  <title>
    <media type="image" width="40px" height="40px" its:translate="no" src="figures/orca-logo.svg" /> Math navigation
  </title>
  <p>
    Explore mathematical expressions and their component parts.
  </p>
  <p>
    Math navigation requires MathCAT, a library for presenting mathematical expressions. To
    start, move to an expression, such as an equation, fraction, or formula, and press <keyseq>
      <key>Orca Modifier</key>
      <key>Alt</key>
      <key>M</key>
    </keyseq>. Press <key>Escape</key> to leave math navigation.
  </p>
  <p>
    An expression contains related parts, such as a fraction's numerator and denominator.
    Movement commands explore these parts; zooming in explores smaller parts and zooming out
    returns to larger structures.
  </p>
  <p>
    The Navigation mode setting selects granularity: Enhanced for meaningful subexpressions,
    Simple for smaller pieces, and Character for individual characters. The granularity commands
    switch among these modes while you explore. Read commands speak the selected part; Describe
    commands give an outline of its structure. Speech mode chooses which of these presentations
    follows a move. In a matrix, cells are the entries arranged in rows and columns.
  </p>
  <p>
    The Where am I commands in math navigation describe your location within the expression,
    rather than your location in the application.
  </p>
  <p>
    You can set numbered place markers to return to, read, or describe parts of an expression.
  </p>
  <section id="settings-math-navigation">
    <title>Settings</title>
    <p>
      <em style="strong">Preferences location:</em>
      <gui>Documents</gui> category, <gui>Math presentation</gui> group.
    </p>
    <p>
      <em style="strong">Available settings:</em>
    </p>
    <list>
      <item>
        <p>
          <gui>Language:</gui> Selects the language Orca
          uses for math presentation.
        </p>
      </item>
      <item>
        <p>
          <gui>Speech style:</gui> Selects the style Orca
          uses when speaking math.
        </p>
      </item>
      <item>
        <p>
          <gui>Verbosity</gui>: Selects how much detail
          Orca speaks for math. Choices: Terse, Medium, Verbose.
        </p>
        <list>
          <item>
            <p>
              <gui>Terse</gui>: Speaks less detail.
            </p>
          </item>
          <item>
            <p>
              <gui>Medium (default)</gui>: Speaks a moderate
              amount of detail.
            </p>
          </item>
          <item>
            <p>
              <gui>Verbose</gui>: Speaks the most detail.
            </p>
          </item>
        </list>
      </item>
      <item>
        <p>
          <gui>Braille code:</gui> Selects the braille
          code Orca uses for mathematical expressions.
        </p>
      </item>
      <item>
        <p>
          <gui>Copy format:</gui> Selects the format used
          when copying math content. Choices: MathML (default), LaTeX, ASCIIMath, Speech.
        </p>
      </item>
      <item>
        <p>
          <gui>Navigation mode:</gui> Selects how Orca
          moves through math during navigation. Choices: Enhanced, Simple, Character.
        </p>
        <list>
          <item>
            <p>
              <gui>Enhanced (default)</gui>: Groups related
              items together for faster navigation.
            </p>
          </item>
          <item>
            <p>
              <gui>Simple</gui>: Visits each math element
              individually.
            </p>
          </item>
          <item>
            <p>
              <gui>Character</gui>: Visits individual
              symbols one at a time.
            </p>
          </item>
        </list>
      </item>
      <item>
        <p>
          <gui>Braille navigation highlight:</gui> Selects how Orca
          marks the current math position in braille. Choices: None, First character, End
          points, All cells.
        </p>
        <list>
          <item>
            <p>
              <gui>None (default)</gui>: Does not mark the
              current math position.
            </p>
          </item>
          <item>
            <p>
              <gui>First character</gui>: Marks the first
              cell of the current math item.
            </p>
          </item>
          <item>
            <p>
              <gui>End points</gui>: Marks the first and
              last cells of the current math item.
            </p>
          </item>
          <item>
            <p>
              <gui>All cells</gui>: Marks every cell of
              the current math item.
            </p>
          </item>
        </list>
      </item>
      <item>
        <p>
          <gui>Automatically exit 2D math structures</gui>: Controls whether
          Orca automatically exits a two-dimensional math structure when you navigate past its
          edge. Default: off.
        </p>
      </item>
    </list>
  </section>
